  "description": "Discontinued, superseded by Gen2. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic Rocket.\n\nYears of production: 2012-2014\n\nThis is the original Rocket, on 26\" wheels. See the Rocket archive for the later generations.\n\nThe Cotic Rocket is our 150mm travel full suspension frame.\n\nThe Rocket is a swaggering speed machine. It brings together the grace, durability, clean lines, fun, interactive feel and attention to detail we put into all our hardtail frames, and adds a whole truckload of speed and rock pounding performance. It's an Enduro race weapon which the Cotic Steel City Media Racing team took to multiple podiums in 2013.\n\nThe Rocket uses a Reynolds 853 front triangle, cromoly seat stays and a 7005-T6 swingarm. They are amazing materials which deliver the durability, strength and confidence a bike like this needs.\n\nThe details are all covered, with ISCG05 mounts, a taper steerer compatible head tube, a 142 x 12 bolt thru back end, and sealed, capped and shielded pivots, right down to the precisely located hose routing.\n\nThe original Rocket with 26\" wheels described here was supplied in 2012 and 2013 with one of the following shock options:\n\nFox Float RL\n\n2012 model year Fox RP23 Factory Kashima\n\n2013 model year Fox CTD Factory Kashima\n\nBOS Vip'r\n\nIn summer 2015 the Rocket got 27.5\" wheels: see the Rocket 275 (Gen2) page.\n\nOwner's manual: download the Cotic Rocket 2012-2013 Owner's Manual (PDF), with details on pivot maintenance, bearing specs and shock set-up.",
